WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.033
Harry: From Christmas
pizzas to "Elf" doughnuts,

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:03.366
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:03.366 --> 00:00:06.300
between fast-food holiday
menus in the US and the UK.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.533
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:09.433 --> 00:00:10.966
Let's start with some
McDonald's seasonal items.

00:00:10.966 --> 00:00:12.900
In the UK we actually
have quite a few of these.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.166
We're going to start
with the chicken Big Mac.

00:00:15.166 --> 00:00:18.333
They brought this into the
UK menu, like, a year ago

00:00:18.333 --> 00:00:20.866
as a kind of temporary thing,
and it was really popular.

00:00:20.866 --> 00:00:24.000
It is a Big Mac, but
instead of the beef patties

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.400
you have chicken patties.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.333
So it goes bun, patty,
lettuce, sauce, pickles,

00:00:28.333 --> 00:00:30.900
the middle bun, the patty, cheese,

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.666
pickles, sauce, and lettuce.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.400
Mm-hmm. Obviously, like,
the ratio, I think,

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.200
of the Big Mac has been
perfected over the years,

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.533
so they haven't messed with that too much.

00:00:41.533 --> 00:00:43.700
My only real complaint is that

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:46.166
instead of an actual
piece of chicken breast,

00:00:46.166 --> 00:00:48.033
it's like a big, very flat chicken nugget.

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:50.600
I also have some questions
as to how festive this is

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.200
and why it's on the festive menu.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.700
Obviously the box is kind
of, like, festive design.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.233
I mean, what is a chicken
if not just a small turkey?

00:00:57.233 --> 00:00:59.766
Next up we have the big and cheesy,

00:00:59.766 --> 00:01:02.166
not the big cheesy, the big and cheesy.

00:01:02.166 --> 00:01:03.733
Look at that.

00:01:03.733 --> 00:01:06.166
And we also have the
big cheesy with bacon.

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:09.400
You have a beef patty, you
have two slices of cheese,

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.733
you have red onions, crispy onions,

00:01:11.733 --> 00:01:14.066
lettuce, and cheese sauce.

00:01:14.066 --> 00:01:16.700
I mean, I like cheese, I
like onions, I like beef.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.166
It's also served in a bun

00:01:18.166 --> 00:01:20.933
which they describe as
"snowflake-flour-dusted,"

00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:22.266
which I guess is maybe their attempt

00:01:22.266 --> 00:01:23.666
at making this actually festive

00:01:23.666 --> 00:01:25.366
and justifying its inclusion on the menu.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.266
Mm. The star of the show for me

00:01:30.266 --> 00:01:32.466
is actually the cheese sauce
that they've added there.

00:01:32.466 --> 00:01:33.333
Personally, I'm a big fan.

00:01:33.333 --> 00:01:35.033
I think it's great. Adds a lovely texture

00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:36.833
and really I guess slightly fake

00:01:36.833 --> 00:01:39.133
but very comforting cheesy
flavor to the burger.

00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:41.266
In the UK at McDonald's we
usually have mozzarella sticks

00:01:41.266 --> 00:01:42.800
as kind of a permanent menu item,

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:44.500
but for Christmas they turn into these,

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:45.766
these cheese melt dippers.

00:01:45.766 --> 00:01:48.000
These are Camembert instead of mozzarella.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.633
They usually come with
a tomato dip as well,

00:01:49.633 --> 00:01:51.033
although I think they forgot ours.

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:52.566
I will usually go out of my way

00:01:52.566 --> 00:01:55.500
to try and find these
around Christmas in the UK.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.266
As with pretty much anything
that is made with fried cheese,

00:01:58.266 --> 00:02:00.400
they're much better eaten fresh and hot.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:04.266
Still a little bit gooey and very tasty.

00:02:04.266 --> 00:02:05.800
Camembert has such a lovely flavor.

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:08.533
I think I consider Brie cheese
festive, strangely enough.

00:02:08.533 --> 00:02:10.366
Not usually Camembert, although
I think it's traditional

00:02:10.366 --> 00:02:12.600
to have a cheese board around Christmas,

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:15.633
so maybe Camembert is included
on that and we can allow it.

00:02:15.633 --> 00:02:16.800
The other hot food option we can get

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.500
but we didn't get today is
the McDonald's chicken combo.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.200
This includes 10 chicken selects,

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.966
which are kind of like
our chicken tenders,

00:02:22.966 --> 00:02:25.500
20 chicken nuggets, four select dips,

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.566
which are like fancier
versions of the dip,

00:02:27.566 --> 00:02:28.866
and then four regular dips.

00:02:28.866 --> 00:02:30.766
It's designed to serve around four people.

00:02:30.766 --> 00:02:33.833
The next menu item is the first
of a kind of themed batch.

00:02:33.833 --> 00:02:36.300
Basically what they've done is
incorporate Galaxy chocolate

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.400
into various McDonald's menu items.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:39.666
Galaxy, for those who don't know,

00:02:39.666 --> 00:02:42.800
is kind of the Mars corporation's
answer to Dairy Milk.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:44.000
There's a bit of a divide in the UK

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.133
as to whether you're Galaxy or Dairy Milk

00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:47.500
when it comes to your milk chocolate.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.666
So, this is the Galaxy caramel pie.

00:02:49.666 --> 00:02:51.400
So what they do is they
take the apple pie shell,

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.800
put some chocolate in that dough, fry it,

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.400
and then instead of the apple sauce

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.233
you have caramel sauce on the inside.

00:02:57.233 --> 00:02:59.833
I mean, I love McDonald's
apple pies. They're so good.

00:02:59.833 --> 00:03:02.000
I don't really want to
mess with the formula.

00:03:06.266 --> 00:03:08.000
I think, for me, I still
just want the apple pie.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.166
I don't think this beats
an apple pie for me.

00:03:10.166 --> 00:03:12.233
Then we have a Galaxy chocolate McFlurry.

00:03:12.233 --> 00:03:13.966
Again, it's just kind
of a standard McFlurry,

00:03:13.966 --> 00:03:17.533
but with these actually
very cute chocolate stars

00:03:17.533 --> 00:03:19.866
which are made of Galaxy chocolate.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:21.466
In addition to the
Galaxy chocolate options,

00:03:21.466 --> 00:03:23.466
they also have Galaxy caramel options.

00:03:23.466 --> 00:03:25.766
You can find these in
the form of the McFlurry,

00:03:25.766 --> 00:03:27.900
but also in the form of a caramel latte

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.966
and also a caramel hot chocolate.

00:03:29.966 --> 00:03:32.966
I'm also not sure why Galaxy
or Galaxy caramel are festive.

00:03:32.966 --> 00:03:34.866
I guess we eat a lot of
chocolate around the holidays.

00:03:34.866 --> 00:03:37.833
But specifically Galaxy? Eh, not so sure.

00:03:37.833 --> 00:03:40.433
I wish our McDonald's had as many

00:03:40.433 --> 00:03:42.433
holiday additions as the UK does,

00:03:42.433 --> 00:03:45.433
but we only have one,
and it's the holiday pie.

00:03:45.433 --> 00:03:48.600
So it's like their regular pie crust

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.466
and what looks like a
bunch of rainbow sprinkles

00:03:51.466 --> 00:03:55.433
and some sort of creamy,
maybe custardy filling.

00:03:55.433 --> 00:03:58.333
What's inside? Well ...

00:03:58.333 --> 00:03:59.900
I don't think this will live up

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:01.566
to the apple pie at all, actually.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.266
Just get the apple pie.

00:04:09.333 --> 00:04:12.633
As always, Starbucks has
gone big for the holidays.

00:04:12.633 --> 00:04:14.366
In the US, you can get a bunch

00:04:14.366 --> 00:04:17.233
of limited-edition food and drink options.

00:04:17.233 --> 00:04:19.233
Let's start with the drinks.

00:04:19.233 --> 00:04:21.000
I love this job!

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:25.100
We have so many hot and iced
drinks, couldn't get them all.

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:28.533
Here is a fantastic
selection of said drinks.

00:04:28.533 --> 00:04:29.933
I'm just going to start down here, y'all.

00:04:29.933 --> 00:04:32.333
The caramel brulée latte.

00:04:35.766 --> 00:04:36.733
Better than you think.

00:04:36.733 --> 00:04:38.466
In other holiday episodes
you've probably seen me

00:04:38.466 --> 00:04:40.000
really "bah, humbug"
a lot of these drinks,

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.700
but maybe I'm getting older,
maybe I'm getting kinder,

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:45.300
or maybe this show has
completely destroyed my palate,

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.366
but either way, I kind of like that.

00:04:47.366 --> 00:04:50.566
Next up, the sugar
cookie almond milk latte.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:55.933
"Sugar cookie" apparently is
just a shorthand for "sweet."

00:04:55.933 --> 00:04:56.866
This is pretty sweet.

00:04:56.866 --> 00:04:58.900
I'm kind of getting an almond
flavor from it in the latte,

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.533
but it really just tastes
like a sweet latte.

00:05:01.533 --> 00:05:04.966
I don't dislike it but, eh, just OK.

00:05:04.966 --> 00:05:08.333
Next up is the chestnut praline latte.

00:05:08.333 --> 00:05:11.733
We've been doing this for three years now,

00:05:11.733 --> 00:05:13.333
this might be the fourth,

00:05:13.333 --> 00:05:16.000
and I still am not quite
clear on what a praline is.

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:20.200
If you handed this to me, I'd be like,

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:23.333
yeah, it's got a kind of
a nutty latte taste to it,

00:05:23.333 --> 00:05:26.166
but I could also see this being
just another almond latte.

00:05:26.166 --> 00:05:28.200
Yeah, these two are very, very similar.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:31.400
Unless you have a taste
for chestnuts and praline

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:33.966
or a chestnut praline, eh, skip it.

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:36.233
Gingerbread latte.

00:05:38.466 --> 00:05:39.533
Yeah, man.

00:05:39.533 --> 00:05:42.300
Very gingerbready. Not to be
confused with just ginger,

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.466
definitely generous with the bread part.

00:05:44.466 --> 00:05:45.933
What?

00:05:45.933 --> 00:05:48.500
Oh, man, these lattes are
hitting, boy. They are hitting.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:51.733
Gingerbread oat milk chai.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.333
I really like this. You're so good.

00:05:58.333 --> 00:06:00.633
The ginger, yes. The bread, yes.

00:06:00.633 --> 00:06:03.100
The oat milk, oh, yeah.
And the chai, oh, the chai.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:06.000
Fantastic. That might be my favorite one.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.400
So, of course you can get this one iced.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.033
Ooh, ice. Look, they even put the little

00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:10.500
nutmeg or whatever on
top. Or is it cinnamon?

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:12.200
What is that? Do you know what that is?

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:14.000
Yeah. Hope that's supposed to be in there.

00:06:15.766 --> 00:06:17.533
No, not as good as this one.

00:06:17.533 --> 00:06:19.966
This, of course, is not the only

00:06:19.966 --> 00:06:21.766
holiday drinks at Starbucks.

00:06:21.766 --> 00:06:24.033
Depending where you are in the world

00:06:24.033 --> 00:06:25.566
or where you are in California,

00:06:25.566 --> 00:06:28.533
or where you are in Burbank,
California, specifically,

00:06:28.533 --> 00:06:30.700
you can get any variety of these.

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:33.600
The Oleato gingerbread oat milk latte,

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:34.600
that's the one with olive oil.

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:36.333
I would suggest you avoid those.

00:06:36.333 --> 00:06:39.233
Iced sugar cookie latte, peppermint mocha,

00:06:39.233 --> 00:06:42.733
white chocolate mocha,
peppermint mocha iced,

00:06:42.733 --> 00:06:44.133
also known as an iced peppermint mocha.

00:06:44.133 --> 00:06:46.200
Caramel brulée Frappuccino,

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:48.166
white chocolate mocha Frappuccino,

00:06:48.166 --> 00:06:52.466
iced caramel brulée latte,
chestnut praline Frappuccino,

00:06:52.466 --> 00:06:53.966
peppermint mocha Frappuccino,

00:06:53.966 --> 00:06:56.233
and an iced peppermint mocha.

00:06:56.233 --> 00:06:58.333
Here are all the Starbucks
exclusive holiday items

00:06:58.333 --> 00:07:00.200
that you'll find in the UK but not the US.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.400
As usual, Starbucks has
gone big for the holidays.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:03.766
A few of these are familiar ones

00:07:03.766 --> 00:07:05.100
that we might have
covered in previous years,

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:06.833
but there are a couple
of new additions as well.

00:07:06.833 --> 00:07:07.666
We'll start with the hot drinks,

00:07:07.666 --> 00:07:08.633
where we have a couple of options

00:07:08.633 --> 00:07:10.200
which you'll only find
around the holidays.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.966
Obviously all of these are also served

00:07:11.966 --> 00:07:14.200
in the Starbucks holiday cup,

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.166
but first we have an eggnog latte.

00:07:16.166 --> 00:07:18.300
This is one that we've
had before in the UK.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.400
Eggnog, not super popular in the UK.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.200
I gather, like, not even
that popular in the US.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:23.333
I think it's just, like, a few people

00:07:23.333 --> 00:07:25.266
are kind of holding on
to it as a tradition.

00:07:26.666 --> 00:07:28.966
It's OK. It's not offensive by any means,

00:07:28.966 --> 00:07:30.900
it's just a sort of spiced,

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.300
almost custardy but just kind of

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:35.033
just like a spiced milky
latte. Doesn't taste of egg.

00:07:35.033 --> 00:07:36.500
Then we have a toffee nut latte,

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:37.833
which is another returning drink.

00:07:40.666 --> 00:07:44.400
God. Every year I get my
hopes up about this one,

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:45.233
thinking it's going to be good,

00:07:45.233 --> 00:07:47.700
because I like toffee, I like nuts,

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:50.433
and then I take my
first sip, and good God.

00:07:50.433 --> 00:07:52.966
If you've ever been
trying to toast hazelnuts,

00:07:52.966 --> 00:07:55.366
for example, and you've burned them,

00:07:55.366 --> 00:07:56.900
that's what this tastes like.

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:59.066
It's just a very sweet latte

00:07:59.066 --> 00:08:00.600
that tastes like burned hazelnuts.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:02.166
Next up we have the caramel waffle latte,

00:08:02.166 --> 00:08:03.900
which is another returner.

00:08:06.966 --> 00:08:08.233
Does it taste of waffle?

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:10.733
Not really.

00:08:10.733 --> 00:08:12.833
I think they almost mean
more like the stroopwafel

00:08:12.833 --> 00:08:14.533
that you might find in the Netherlands

00:08:14.533 --> 00:08:16.800
rather than a sort of breakfast waffle,

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:18.633
but it doesn't really taste
of either of those things,

00:08:18.633 --> 00:08:19.966
it just kind of tastes of caramel.

00:08:19.966 --> 00:08:21.400
So those first three
drinks we've had before,

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.500
but we have two new drinks this year.

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:26.133
Firstly, we have the hazelnut
crunch hot chocolate.

00:08:28.933 --> 00:08:30.466
Hm, OK.

00:08:30.466 --> 00:08:34.000
So, there are things floating in it,

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:36.500
which I think at one point
might have been crunchy.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.400
However, you don't have
to be a genius to know

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:41.066
that when you put
crunchy things in liquid,

00:08:41.066 --> 00:08:42.633
they often soften.

00:08:42.633 --> 00:08:45.366
Maybe go back to the
research and development

00:08:45.366 --> 00:08:47.733
until you can find a
hydrophobic crunchy substance.

00:08:47.733 --> 00:08:49.033
And then our next new drink

00:08:49.033 --> 00:08:51.266
is the chocolaty gingerbread latte.

00:08:51.266 --> 00:08:52.766
Let's see how they've managed to

00:08:52.766 --> 00:08:55.100
marry these three beverages.

00:08:57.866 --> 00:08:59.733
Not well is the answer to that.

00:08:59.733 --> 00:09:01.266
[crew laughs]

00:09:01.266 --> 00:09:03.566
It's mostly gingerbread
with a kind of, like,

00:09:03.566 --> 00:09:05.033
that bitterness from the coffee.

00:09:05.033 --> 00:09:07.900
Also, just a quick note, if you
have the venti eggnog latte,

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:10.333
that contains 52.8 grams of sugar,

00:09:10.333 --> 00:09:13.600
which is more than 100% of
your daily recommended intake.

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:15.933
Probably my last eggnog
latte of the season.

00:09:15.933 --> 00:09:18.133
And for the festive treats
at Starbucks in the US,

00:09:18.133 --> 00:09:20.400
you can get, in no particular order,

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:23.033
this peppermint brownie cake pop.

00:09:23.966 --> 00:09:26.933
The Cranberry Bliss Bar. We got a slice;

00:09:26.933 --> 00:09:30.466
you can also get this in
its whole tray in box form.

00:09:30.466 --> 00:09:33.566
And a sugarplum cheese Danish.

00:09:34.966 --> 00:09:36.466
You know, I'm curious about this cake pop.

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:42.533
Yeah, that's nice. I like that.

00:09:48.166 --> 00:09:49.000
So good.

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:54.800
I'm not getting sugarplum
specifically out of it,

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:55.733
but, yeah, cheese Danish

00:09:55.733 --> 00:09:57.066
with a nice little jam in the center.

00:09:57.066 --> 00:09:58.100
Why not, right?

00:09:58.100 --> 00:09:59.600
Also, depending where
you are in the country,

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:02.666
you can get a snowman cookie
or a gingerbread loaf.

00:10:02.666 --> 00:10:03.766
This year I think we might actually have

00:10:03.766 --> 00:10:06.300
more festive items than
America, which is pretty cool.

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:07.533
Doesn't happen often on "Food Wars."

00:10:07.533 --> 00:10:09.033
We'll start with the sandwiches.

00:10:09.033 --> 00:10:12.066
Here we have a turkey
and chicken sandwich.

00:10:12.066 --> 00:10:15.900
There's also bacon, some
stuffing, some cranberry sauce,

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:17.233
as well as some spinach in there.

00:10:17.233 --> 00:10:19.800
It seems a bit weird to
combine very similar meats.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:22.233
I guess maybe people make a turducken

00:10:22.233 --> 00:10:23.066
and all that sort of stuff,

00:10:23.066 --> 00:10:24.366
but I think just have one or the other.

00:10:24.366 --> 00:10:26.466
Just have, like, a good turkey sandwich.

00:10:26.466 --> 00:10:28.966
Next up, we have the holiday ham sub roll.

00:10:28.966 --> 00:10:31.033
Sub roll, submarine roll,

00:10:31.033 --> 00:10:32.566
because the bun is supposed to look

00:10:32.566 --> 00:10:34.200
slightly like a submarine.

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.833
This one has honey-roast ham,
mature cheddar cheese, honey,

00:10:36.833 --> 00:10:39.766
and a mustard slaw with
cranberry chutney and spinach.

00:10:39.766 --> 00:10:42.633
The default seems to be adding
spinach and cranberry chutney

00:10:42.633 --> 00:10:44.133
to all of these to make them festive.

00:10:44.133 --> 00:10:46.033
I'm slightly more into
the hot sandwich options,

00:10:46.033 --> 00:10:49.566
so here we have the
pigs-under-blankets sandwich.

00:10:49.566 --> 00:10:51.233
[grunts]

00:10:51.233 --> 00:10:53.200
Obviously in the UK we
have pigs in blankets,

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:55.200
which are sausages wrapped in bacon,

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:56.700
rather than the American way,

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:59.000
which is wrapping a
sausage in some pastry.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:00.200
These aren't pigs in blankets

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:01.700
because the sausages aren't wrapped.

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:03.233
They are pigs under
blankets because I think

00:11:03.233 --> 00:11:05.966
the bacon is added as a
separate layer on top,

00:11:05.966 --> 00:11:09.733
although it's kind of
hermetically sealed itself

00:11:09.733 --> 00:11:11.400
to the bread and I can't get it off.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:13.166
We've obviously got the
sausages and the bacon here,

00:11:13.166 --> 00:11:15.600
but there's also some cheddar
cheese, some stuffing,

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:16.966
some cranberry sauce as well.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:23.400
It's gone a little bit
dry now that it's cold,

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:24.633
but I actually quite like that.

00:11:24.633 --> 00:11:26.666
I think the bread is good.
It's crunchy on the outside

00:11:26.666 --> 00:11:28.100
but nice and chewy on the inside.

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:29.800
The pork sausages have a good flavor.

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:32.000
You could even go more
generous with the mayo.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.133
And I think that's actually a
pretty good festive sandwich.

00:11:34.133 --> 00:11:36.900
Next up we have the Brie
and cranberry focaccia.

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:38.966
I think this used to be
called the cranmerry focaccia,

00:11:38.966 --> 00:11:40.566
but they've changed it

00:11:40.566 --> 00:11:42.400
and just gone straight down the middle,

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:43.600
let people know what they're getting.

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:45.433
It's a sandwich with some Brie,

00:11:45.433 --> 00:11:47.533
the cranberry chutney, more spinach again.

00:11:47.533 --> 00:11:50.233
They must have a surplus
of spinach this year.

00:11:50.233 --> 00:11:52.700
And it's all served on
this rosemary focaccia.

00:11:55.733 --> 00:11:57.600
The focaccia is really dry.

00:11:57.600 --> 00:11:59.533
That might be mitigated
if you eat it in store

00:11:59.533 --> 00:12:00.933
and it's freshly heated.

00:12:00.933 --> 00:12:02.800
But, like, the pigs-under-blankets roll

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:04.800
still kind of held up, whereas that is

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:07.400
quite difficult to eat
when it's cold, so ...

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:09.366
And then the final hot option we have

00:12:09.366 --> 00:12:11.833
is the festive feast panini.

00:12:11.833 --> 00:12:13.000
Ta-da!

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.300
Firstly, this is actually chicken,

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:15.233
this isn't turkey.

00:12:15.233 --> 00:12:18.133
We have bacon, there's some stuffing,

00:12:18.133 --> 00:12:19.733
there's a turkey gravy on here,

00:12:19.733 --> 00:12:21.166
some cranberry sauce as well,

00:12:21.166 --> 00:12:22.900
and then it's all kind of melted together

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:24.466
with some cheddar cheese.

00:12:24.466 --> 00:12:25.566
We love a panini in the UK.

00:12:25.566 --> 00:12:28.000
They're really popular on café menus

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:29.266
as a hot sandwich option.

00:12:31.066 --> 00:12:32.733
The fillings work pretty well together.

00:12:32.733 --> 00:12:33.933
Again, could probably stand to go

00:12:33.933 --> 00:12:35.033
for slightly more moisture,

00:12:35.033 --> 00:12:37.433
I think the theme has just
been a bit dry so far.

00:12:37.433 --> 00:12:38.400
And then we have some sweet

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.133
baked seasonal goods from Starbucks.

00:12:40.133 --> 00:12:43.266
I'm going to request a quick
in memoriam section here

00:12:43.266 --> 00:12:45.633
because for the first time in
a few years of doing these,

00:12:45.633 --> 00:12:47.233
we don't have South Pole Sam.

00:12:47.233 --> 00:12:49.466
My son has vanished.

00:12:49.466 --> 00:12:51.033
I'm hoping it's a brief hiatus

00:12:51.033 --> 00:12:52.733
rather than a permanent goodbye.

00:12:52.733 --> 00:12:54.500
I hope he's good wherever he is,

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:55.866
with North Pole Nat as well.

00:12:55.866 --> 00:12:58.066
Hope they're living off
their dreams together.

00:12:58.066 --> 00:12:59.300
This one's for you, buddy.

00:13:00.733 --> 00:13:01.933
Starbucks does have quite a few

00:13:01.933 --> 00:13:04.100
baked-good options here
in the UK for Christmas.

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:05.700
We have the Christmas tree brownie.

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:06.633
Does what it says on the tin.

00:13:06.633 --> 00:13:08.366
It's a brownie in the
shape of a Christmas tree.

00:13:08.366 --> 00:13:10.400
We have the caramel waffle muffin.

00:13:10.400 --> 00:13:11.833
This is what I was talking about

00:13:11.833 --> 00:13:14.500
when I said the caramel waffle latte

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:16.166
I think was based on these.

00:13:16.166 --> 00:13:18.700
So, this is what the Dutch
would call a stroopwafel.

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:22.533
It's these very thin,
almost biscuity layers

00:13:22.533 --> 00:13:24.400
with a layer of caramel inside.

00:13:26.266 --> 00:13:27.266
If you go to Amsterdam,

00:13:27.266 --> 00:13:29.000
get yourself some fresh stroopwafels.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:29.833
You'll have a good time.

00:13:31.133 --> 00:13:32.800
Then you also have some toffee icing,

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:34.566
and then inside there's some molten toffee

00:13:34.566 --> 00:13:36.233
in the middle as well.
It's a pretty good muffin.

00:13:36.233 --> 00:13:39.600
This is the toffee nut cookie,
or at least half of it.

00:13:42.566 --> 00:13:44.800
Then finally we have two cookie options.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:47.466
We have, of course, the
classic Starbucks bearista,

00:13:47.466 --> 00:13:49.833
but he's been given a holiday makeover.

00:13:51.966 --> 00:13:54.800
Domino's has brought back
its Christmas pizza for 2023.

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:55.700
The fact that they've brought this back

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:57.600
does suggest that some
people are actually buying it

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:59.033
and that it's a commercial
success for them,

00:13:59.033 --> 00:14:00.766
which I'm a little bit confused by

00:14:00.766 --> 00:14:02.800
because I don't think I've
ever enjoyed this thing.

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:04.433
Its official name is the festive one,

00:14:04.433 --> 00:14:07.433
and it contains a cranberry
drizzle, some bacon rashers,

00:14:07.433 --> 00:14:10.966
some pulled sage and onion
turkey, onions, and sausage.

00:14:10.966 --> 00:14:13.200
Weirdly, the thing I
probably object to the most

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:14.733
is the red onion on here.

00:14:14.733 --> 00:14:17.133
The cranberry sauce I can
almost kind of deal with.

00:14:20.266 --> 00:14:22.866
I don't remember exactly how
I reacted to it last time,

00:14:22.866 --> 00:14:24.200
but it's very sweet.

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:25.800
I will say I quite like
the flavor of the turkey.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:26.933
You definitely get the sage and onion,

00:14:26.933 --> 00:14:28.666
which is what we would typically include

00:14:28.666 --> 00:14:30.066
in stuffing in the UK.

00:14:30.066 --> 00:14:32.533
And the sausage and the
bacon are just kind of there.

00:14:32.533 --> 00:14:35.400
I just think there is way
better pizzas on the menu.

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:36.366
The best thing I can say about it

00:14:36.366 --> 00:14:38.300
is that I think it looks quite pretty.

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:39.433
What actually does kind of excite me

00:14:39.433 --> 00:14:40.400
on the Domino's menu, though,

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:42.433
is their new seasonal desserts.

00:14:42.433 --> 00:14:45.366
These are their twisted
chocolate cinnamon dough balls.

00:14:45.366 --> 00:14:47.233
I think basically what they
do is just take their dough,

00:14:47.233 --> 00:14:49.433
twist it into these kind of
twisted dough ball shapes,

00:14:49.433 --> 00:14:51.633
bake it, and then top it
with various seasonings.

00:14:51.633 --> 00:14:55.466
In this case there's chocolate
sauce and cinnamon sugar.

00:14:55.466 --> 00:14:58.433
I mean, I love dough balls,
I love chocolate sauce,

00:14:58.433 --> 00:14:59.533
and I love cinnamon, so ...

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:04.933
Mm-hmm.

00:15:04.933 --> 00:15:06.400
I love the texture of dough balls.

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:07.666
I love the crunch on the outside

00:15:07.666 --> 00:15:09.000
and the chew you get in the middle.

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:11.433
I think if I were ordering at
Domino's in the festive period

00:15:11.433 --> 00:15:14.366
and I wanted to feel festive,
I would swerve the pizza

00:15:14.366 --> 00:15:15.366
and instead just get these.

00:15:17.366 --> 00:15:19.066
When it comes to the holiday season,

00:15:19.066 --> 00:15:22.500
the US loves to add peppermint
into pretty much everything,

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:24.400
and Wendy's is no exception.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:27.866
So we have the peppermint
Frosty cream cold brew

00:15:27.866 --> 00:15:30.100
and the actual peppermint Frosty.

00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:34.133
I've never had Wendy's coffee
before, so I'm very intrigued.

00:15:36.166 --> 00:15:38.366
I actually like the taste of the coffee,

00:15:38.366 --> 00:15:40.933
I just feel like there's
very little flavor payoff

00:15:40.933 --> 00:15:43.733
from the Frosty that's
added into the coffee.

00:15:43.733 --> 00:15:45.400
I'm mostly tasting coffee.

00:15:46.233 --> 00:15:50.066
Moving on, we're going to try
the actual peppermint Frosty.

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:58.333
It basically tastes like
a less serious version

00:15:58.333 --> 00:16:00.300
of mint chocolate chip ice cream,

00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:02.500
so it just has no chocolate chips

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:05.100
and it's just the ice cream
part. It's pretty good.

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:07.766
It's not my favorite Frosty
flavor I've ever tried,

00:16:07.766 --> 00:16:10.500
but it's a fun holiday flavor.

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:14.100
KFC has also added a few new things

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:15.966
to its Christmas menu in the UK this year.

00:16:15.966 --> 00:16:18.066
We'll start with this,
the gravy triple bucket.

00:16:18.066 --> 00:16:19.900
It's one big sharing item.

00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:21.600
In here you get, bear with me,

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:23.733
six pieces of Original Recipe chicken,

00:16:23.733 --> 00:16:26.166
one regular popcorn
chicken, eight hot wings,

00:16:26.166 --> 00:16:29.033
six mini fillets, two large gravy sides,

00:16:29.033 --> 00:16:31.233
four fries, and a drink,

00:16:31.233 --> 00:16:33.900
and it comes with instructions
to "let the gravy flow."

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:35.266
The bucket's quite fun.

00:16:35.266 --> 00:16:37.233
Otherwise, they haven't
made too much effort.

00:16:37.233 --> 00:16:38.400
They actually made a point this year

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:40.166
of kind of addressing the demands

00:16:40.166 --> 00:16:42.066
for them to do turkey at Christmas,

00:16:42.066 --> 00:16:43.433
and just said that, "Actually, no.

00:16:43.433 --> 00:16:45.100
We do chicken. We're going
to stick to our guns.

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:46.133
Stick to what we know best."

00:16:46.133 --> 00:16:48.900
This whole thing will set
you back around £28.99,

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:50.300
which is quite a lot of money,

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:51.900
although I think it's
probably designed to be shared

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:54.066
between four or five people,

00:16:54.066 --> 00:16:56.333
so per-person cost, not too bad.

00:16:56.333 --> 00:16:58.600
We have two festive burger
options, starting with this one,

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:01.366
the stuffing tower burger.
So, usually at the UK KFC,

00:17:01.366 --> 00:17:03.066
we will have a tower burger on the menu.

00:17:03.066 --> 00:17:04.900
However, outside the festive period,

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:06.833
this just means that
they've added a hash brown

00:17:06.833 --> 00:17:08.300
into a regular chicken burger.

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:09.366
For the festive period, however,

00:17:09.366 --> 00:17:13.466
the hash brown is gone, and
it's been replaced by this,

00:17:13.466 --> 00:17:16.400
which is a sage and onion stuffing patty.

00:17:16.400 --> 00:17:17.766
I will say, looking at the color of this,

00:17:17.766 --> 00:17:19.900
that doesn't look like any
sage and onion stuffing

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:21.833
that I've ever had in my entire life.

00:17:21.833 --> 00:17:25.100
We have some cranberry sauce
for some extra festive twang,

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:26.600
and that's all layered on top

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:29.000
of a pretty regular KFC chicken sandwich.

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:31.933
So you have a cheesy chicken fillet,

00:17:31.933 --> 00:17:33.500
some lettuce, and some mayo.

00:17:36.966 --> 00:17:41.700
I do not think that a patty
is the optimal delivery form

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:43.700
for sage and onion stuffing.

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:45.966
I say bring back the hash browns.

00:17:45.966 --> 00:17:48.900
And the other option is the
stuffing stacker burger.

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:51.033
So, a stacker burger in the UK at KFC

00:17:51.033 --> 00:17:53.000
is basically just a double burger.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:55.166
As you can see, it's got two of these

00:17:55.166 --> 00:17:57.000
chicken fillets with the cheese.

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:59.700
And, once again, our old friend,

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:00.966
the stuffing patty.

00:18:00.966 --> 00:18:02.300
I think for a chain that's clearly put

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:04.200
some thought into their
Christmas offerings,

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:06.733
in terms of the packaging

00:18:06.733 --> 00:18:10.266
and including things like
cranberry sauce and stuffing,

00:18:10.266 --> 00:18:11.966
I think I'm disappointed
with the end result.

00:18:11.966 --> 00:18:14.933
KFC, of course, has a
few festive menu items,

00:18:14.933 --> 00:18:17.200
nothing really in the chicken department.

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:19.000
What they do have, and
they do this every year,

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:21.933
is a festive bucket for the chicken.

00:18:21.933 --> 00:18:24.166
It looks cool. I think
they always do a good job

00:18:24.166 --> 00:18:25.133
with the design on this.

00:18:25.133 --> 00:18:27.666
You got a sentient bucket of chicken there

00:18:27.666 --> 00:18:29.233
with arms and legs. That's bizarre.

00:18:29.233 --> 00:18:30.700
If you see the drum playing itself

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:33.100
with drumsticks, wah-wah-wah,

00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:35.966
and of course the centerpiece
is this really cool tree.

00:18:35.966 --> 00:18:39.266
I'm not complaining, because
look what's in the bucket.

00:18:39.266 --> 00:18:40.533
I want to say I would've liked to see them

00:18:40.533 --> 00:18:43.100
maybe introduce some
sort of limited-edition,

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:45.400
I don't know, Christmas extra spicy.

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:48.333
I don't know. Hey, I
don't work at R&amp;D for KFC,

00:18:48.333 --> 00:18:50.600
so I'm sure there's a reason
they didn't do it. Money.

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:52.733
The only new menu item is this.

00:18:52.733 --> 00:18:55.200
It is the mac and cheese chicken wrap.

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:57.900
Come on. It was already in every store.

00:18:57.900 --> 00:18:59.066
Let's just put it on the menu.

00:18:59.066 --> 00:19:01.500
Wraps, had them. Chicken, had it.

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:02.766
Mac and cheese, had it.

00:19:02.766 --> 00:19:04.733
Put it together, new menu item!

00:19:07.433 --> 00:19:09.566
I mean, who am I kidding? That's great.

00:19:09.566 --> 00:19:10.766
It's their chicken,
it's crispy, I love it.

00:19:10.766 --> 00:19:12.466
It's their mac and cheese, which is great.

00:19:12.466 --> 00:19:15.133
It's in a wrap, which I don't
object to really, so ...

00:19:15.133 --> 00:19:18.233
Speaking of not-holiday-specific,
at least I don't think,

00:19:18.233 --> 00:19:21.000
there's the colonel's homestyle brownie.

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:23.933
Yo, brownies. I mean, could this be

00:19:23.933 --> 00:19:25.733
on the menu all year round? Yeah.

00:19:25.733 --> 00:19:27.133
But just the holidays, fine.

00:19:28.033 --> 00:19:30.733
KFC always releases supercool
merch around the holidays.

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:35.200
I was given a budget of up to $40,

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:36.533
and the only thing that I could get

00:19:36.533 --> 00:19:37.566
that fell into that budget

00:19:37.566 --> 00:19:40.633
was this fun holiday bucket hat.

00:19:40.633 --> 00:19:41.900
Same idea as the bucket.

00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:45.433
You got a tree, you got a
snowman, you got french fries,

00:19:45.433 --> 00:19:48.600
and you got these guys making a snowman,

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:50.433
and then you got what
appears to be a snowman

00:19:50.433 --> 00:19:52.333
that is self-aware.

00:19:52.333 --> 00:19:54.233
I just don't like wearing hats, really.

00:19:54.233 --> 00:19:56.100
This is as far down as I can get it.

00:19:56.100 --> 00:19:58.466
Both of my coworkers are laughing at me,

00:19:58.466 --> 00:19:59.966
so I can only assume I look great.

00:19:59.966 --> 00:20:02.100
Let's be honest, internet.
Let's get a poll going.

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:03.366
Can I rock this look?

00:20:03.366 --> 00:20:07.133
Holiday stuff aside, is
Joe a bucket-hat guy?

00:20:07.133 --> 00:20:08.400
Where are my bucket-hat-heads at?

00:20:08.400 --> 00:20:09.833
In the comments, let me know.

00:20:09.833 --> 00:20:12.800
New look, or put it in the trash?

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:14.700
Honestly, I think that
merch looks kind of sick,

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:15.866
and I kind of want some.

00:20:15.866 --> 00:20:17.200
KFC, you know where to find me.

00:20:19.133 --> 00:20:22.400
Here are all of our exclusive
festive drinks from Dunkin'.

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:26.400
So, the first drink we have is
the cookie butter cold brew.

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:27.933
It has this stuff at the bottom

00:20:27.933 --> 00:20:32.933
that I think is the cookie
butter syrup, but it's very dark.

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:38.533
I mean, it's good, but like
every other drink at Dunkin',

00:20:38.533 --> 00:20:40.000
it is very, very sweet.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:43.033
I do like that cookie butter
syrup, though. It's tasty.

00:20:43.033 --> 00:20:44.500
It tastes like a gingerbread cookie.

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:48.333
This is an iced toasted
white chocolate latte.

00:20:50.300 --> 00:20:53.200
It kind of tastes a little coconutty

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:55.133
but also a little buttery.

00:20:55.133 --> 00:20:57.566
It's very odd. I don't love it.

00:20:58.533 --> 00:21:00.466
Somebody out there will, though.

00:21:00.466 --> 00:21:02.200
This is an iced peppermint mocha.

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:06.333
I love peppermint mocha, so
I'm hoping it's delicious.

00:21:06.333 --> 00:21:07.866
I never get them iced, though.

00:21:07.866 --> 00:21:09.433
I think they taste better hot.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:13.200
Yeah, that's really good.

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:14.966
I'm surprised that the peppermint syrup

00:21:14.966 --> 00:21:17.433
isn't as strong as other
peppermint mochas I've had

00:21:17.433 --> 00:21:19.933
from other places,
because Dunkin' is known

00:21:19.933 --> 00:21:23.766
for doing the most with the
syrups and all the flavors,

00:21:23.766 --> 00:21:26.766
but this one's actually pretty mellow.

00:21:26.766 --> 00:21:30.000
This is the spiced cookie
coffee, and I want it to be good.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:32.700
I love spiced cookies. I
love gingerbread cookies.

00:21:35.166 --> 00:21:36.166
It's not bad.

00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:39.666
I think it needs some
sort of creamy element

00:21:39.666 --> 00:21:42.866
to make it actually come together.

00:21:42.866 --> 00:21:46.866
This is that same spiced
cookie coffee, except it's hot.

00:21:46.866 --> 00:21:48.733
I think it'll taste better this way.

00:21:52.066 --> 00:21:53.333
Yeah, I think I'm right.

00:21:53.333 --> 00:21:56.300
Next, we have a hot
chocolate with peppermint.

00:21:59.133 --> 00:22:03.466
That has a weird aftertaste
that I don't like.

00:22:03.466 --> 00:22:04.800
So, this is a hot chocolate

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:07.266
with the toasted white chocolate syrup.

00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:12.766
Same thing. What is going on

00:22:12.766 --> 00:22:14.833
with the Dunkin' hot chocolates?

00:22:14.833 --> 00:22:17.500
Why are they so oily-tasting?

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:20.066
This is the brown sugar cookie iced chai.

00:22:20.066 --> 00:22:21.066
This looks really good.

00:22:21.066 --> 00:22:23.100
I feel like this looks like a good color.

00:22:23.100 --> 00:22:24.633
This is the difference between

00:22:24.633 --> 00:22:26.700
a coffee that you know is going to be bad

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:28.266
and something that looks pretty good.

00:22:28.266 --> 00:22:31.200
This color theory only applies
to Dunkin', by the way.

00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:32.966
I feel like if you go to Dunkin' a lot,

00:22:32.966 --> 00:22:34.466
you know exactly what I'm talking about.

00:22:37.100 --> 00:22:40.066
Delicious. Delicious,
delicious, wonderful.

00:22:40.066 --> 00:22:41.566
It is a little overly sweet.

00:22:41.566 --> 00:22:43.300
I've just come to get used to that

00:22:43.300 --> 00:22:47.166
when it comes to Dunkin'
anything, but this is really good.

00:22:47.166 --> 00:22:49.000
This is the exact same thing but hot,

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:50.966
the brown sugar cookie chai.

00:22:52.400 --> 00:22:55.466
Whoa, no. Iced, it's really delicious.

00:22:55.466 --> 00:22:58.500
This is the toasted white
chocolate coconut cold brew.

00:22:58.500 --> 00:23:00.466
I'm not a huge fan of coconut.

00:23:01.800 --> 00:23:02.900
That's not bad.

00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:04.666
I do feel like with some of these drinks,

00:23:04.666 --> 00:23:06.300
the iced version is the way to go

00:23:06.300 --> 00:23:08.700
just because it helps it not be so sweet.

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:11.400
This is the brown sugar
cookie frozen coffee.

00:23:11.400 --> 00:23:13.766
I love all of the Dunkin' frozen coffees.

00:23:13.766 --> 00:23:17.366
I think they're so tasty, and
they're basically Coolattas.

00:23:17.366 --> 00:23:19.200
They just don't call it that anymore.

00:23:19.200 --> 00:23:20.800
This is so yummy.

00:23:20.800 --> 00:23:23.866
Next, we have the toasted
white chocolate iced coffee.

00:23:23.866 --> 00:23:25.433
This looks like a pretty good color.

00:23:25.433 --> 00:23:26.900
Are we seeing the color theory?

00:23:26.900 --> 00:23:28.266
Are we seeing what I mean?

00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:32.800
So, at Dunkin', if you get
something with a swirl,

00:23:32.800 --> 00:23:36.100
that means it's a
sweetened flavor additive,

00:23:36.100 --> 00:23:37.500
versus the flavor shots,

00:23:37.500 --> 00:23:40.033
which are just the flavor
with no added sugar.

00:23:40.033 --> 00:23:42.333
I kind of prefer those to the swirls

00:23:42.333 --> 00:23:45.033
just because you can
overdo the swirls so easily

00:23:45.033 --> 00:23:46.800
and the whole thing
just becomes too sweet,

00:23:46.800 --> 00:23:49.466
but this one is actually
a pretty good balance.

00:23:49.466 --> 00:23:50.533
And last but not least,

00:23:50.533 --> 00:23:52.833
we have a peppermint mocha hot coffee.

00:23:55.400 --> 00:23:57.233
The cream that's in it isn't doing enough

00:23:57.233 --> 00:24:01.233
to make it a creamy,
full-bodied kind of beverage.

00:24:01.233 --> 00:24:02.566
It's too watery.

00:24:04.400 --> 00:24:08.100
I got it on my pants. Help!

00:24:08.100 --> 00:24:09.300
And here we have all of the

00:24:09.300 --> 00:24:11.700
festive food exclusives at Dunkin'.

00:24:11.700 --> 00:24:14.166
I'm going to start with
these loaded hash browns.

00:24:14.166 --> 00:24:15.533
They're calling my name.

00:24:15.533 --> 00:24:18.166
I'm a big fan of Dunkin' hash browns.

00:24:18.166 --> 00:24:20.033
So, this is just their regular hash browns

00:24:20.033 --> 00:24:22.266
covered with jalapeño cheddar queso

00:24:22.266 --> 00:24:24.600
and some chopped-up bacon bits.

00:24:24.600 --> 00:24:26.633
This smells amazing.

00:24:26.633 --> 00:24:28.933
And it's all congealed.
Just give me a moment.

00:24:32.900 --> 00:24:35.666
I do wish that there was a better ratio

00:24:35.666 --> 00:24:37.766
of queso to actual hash browns.

00:24:37.766 --> 00:24:39.500
It's all a little bit dry.

00:24:39.500 --> 00:24:42.300
It's a little salty, but
it tastes good to me.

00:24:42.300 --> 00:24:45.400
Like, I could eat this
whole thing in five minutes.

00:24:45.400 --> 00:24:47.100
Moving on, we have two wraps.

00:24:47.100 --> 00:24:48.833
One of these is chorizo and egg,

00:24:48.833 --> 00:24:51.366
and the other is chicken
and roasted pepper.

00:24:51.366 --> 00:24:55.133
I'm not sure which is which,
so let's taste them both.

00:24:55.133 --> 00:24:56.300
Let's start with this one,

00:24:56.300 --> 00:25:00.133
the one that's not a
radioactive orange color.

00:25:03.000 --> 00:25:05.266
It's not bad. I think it's
missing a bit of salt,

00:25:05.266 --> 00:25:07.166
but it's actually got a nice heat to it,

00:25:07.166 --> 00:25:09.900
which I wasn't expecting.
I would order this.

00:25:09.900 --> 00:25:12.400
I'm assuming that this
is the chorizo and egg,

00:25:12.400 --> 00:25:16.700
so let's taste it. Why it's so orange,

00:25:16.700 --> 00:25:18.033
don't know.

00:25:18.033 --> 00:25:19.900
We dye everything in this country, OK?

00:25:19.900 --> 00:25:21.766
We dye all of our food.

00:25:25.700 --> 00:25:29.800
Hm, I feel like it's a little bland.

00:25:29.800 --> 00:25:33.366
I can't really taste much of
anything besides the chorizo.

00:25:33.366 --> 00:25:35.800
This is the maple sugar snackin' bacon.

00:25:35.800 --> 00:25:37.400
Dunkin' is the only place

00:25:37.400 --> 00:25:39.966
I've ever seen offer bacon like this,

00:25:39.966 --> 00:25:43.733
like, just a little pack of to-go bacon.

00:25:43.733 --> 00:25:45.533
I assume it's going to be sweet.

00:25:48.233 --> 00:25:50.400
Yeah, just tastes like sweet bacon.

00:25:50.400 --> 00:25:52.566
It's kind of soggy.

00:25:52.566 --> 00:25:56.866
It's bacon. It's going to
taste good. And it does.

00:25:56.866 --> 00:25:58.166
I'm going to eat one more piece.

00:25:59.666 --> 00:26:01.533
Next, we have the maple sugar bacon

00:26:01.533 --> 00:26:03.366
breakfast sandwich on a croissant.

00:26:03.366 --> 00:26:06.500
I really love getting Dunkin'
sandwiches on a croissant.

00:26:06.500 --> 00:26:08.700
I think they toast them really well.

00:26:08.700 --> 00:26:10.800
Maybe this one's a
little too well toasted.

00:26:10.800 --> 00:26:12.066
It's a little burned.

00:26:12.066 --> 00:26:14.766
Oh, you guys, that's a little ...

00:26:14.766 --> 00:26:17.933
Oh, no. I think after opening it,

00:26:17.933 --> 00:26:19.533
I don't want to take a bite of it,

00:26:19.533 --> 00:26:21.900
so let's just move on to the next thing.

00:26:21.900 --> 00:26:24.366
This is the ham and
Swiss croissant stuffer.

00:26:24.366 --> 00:26:25.766
So, what I think they did

00:26:25.766 --> 00:26:29.566
is just baked the ham and
Swiss inside the croissant

00:26:29.566 --> 00:26:31.766
and then baked the
croissant instead of just

00:26:31.766 --> 00:26:34.433
putting it into a croissant
sandwich like this.

00:26:34.433 --> 00:26:37.433
I'm going to go for the middle
because I want the filling.

00:26:41.233 --> 00:26:42.766
That was such a deep bite,

00:26:42.766 --> 00:26:46.066
and I didn't get a lick of
that ham or that cheese.

00:26:47.333 --> 00:26:51.733
I just want to -- oh, it's like deli ham.

00:26:51.733 --> 00:26:53.166
I'm going to taste the ham.

00:26:56.700 --> 00:26:59.233
I would never get it again, but it's fine.

00:26:59.233 --> 00:27:01.766
One thing we're missing is
the triple-chocolate muffin,

00:27:01.766 --> 00:27:03.800
which I ordered, but it didn't come,

00:27:03.800 --> 00:27:05.733
so I guess they ran out.

00:27:05.733 --> 00:27:08.133
It is a holiday exclusive
at Dunkin', though.

00:27:10.166 --> 00:27:13.966
Krispy Kreme is celebrating
the 20th anniversary

00:27:13.966 --> 00:27:18.266
of the movie "Elf" with
"Elf" doughnut collections.

00:27:18.266 --> 00:27:21.900
I love it. I love "Elf." I just
think this is just the best.

00:27:21.900 --> 00:27:24.033
Apparently Will Ferrell
held out for more money,

00:27:24.033 --> 00:27:27.633
because he's not involved
in this holiday branding.

00:27:27.633 --> 00:27:30.900
Fantastic movie. Twenty years
ago? Oh, God, I'm so old.

00:27:30.900 --> 00:27:34.066
Anyway, let's take a
look at the doughnuts.

00:27:34.066 --> 00:27:35.600
The Buddy snow globe doughnut,

00:27:35.600 --> 00:27:37.066
the Buddy makes breakfast doughnut,

00:27:37.066 --> 00:27:38.266
the Christmas lights doughnut,

00:27:38.266 --> 00:27:40.800
and the Santa belly doughnut.

00:27:40.800 --> 00:27:43.566
This is just so great. Isn't
this great? This is great.

00:27:43.566 --> 00:27:44.700
So that's another Buddy one.

00:27:44.700 --> 00:27:47.500
And again, really smart,
just the hat and the feet.

00:27:47.500 --> 00:27:50.500
Don't need Will Ferrell. The Santa belly.

00:27:50.500 --> 00:27:52.366
This is probably a
cream-filled one, right?

00:27:57.066 --> 00:27:59.466
[sighs] Krispy Kreme is so good.

00:27:59.466 --> 00:28:03.000
I could eat this whole
box while watching "Elf,"

00:28:03.000 --> 00:28:05.833
and the second it ends,
being sad that "Elf" is over

00:28:05.833 --> 00:28:08.500
and sad that I ate 12 doughnuts
will put me into a funk.

00:28:08.500 --> 00:28:12.233
Hey, Krispy Kreme, fantastic.

00:28:12.233 --> 00:28:14.433
And, of course, there are
limited-edition drinks

00:28:14.433 --> 00:28:16.666
at Krispy Kreme this holiday season.

00:28:16.666 --> 00:28:18.466
The main one is the sugar cookie latte,

00:28:18.466 --> 00:28:21.000
which you can get hot, iced, or frozen.

00:28:21.000 --> 00:28:23.666
And that, of course, is none of these!

00:28:23.666 --> 00:28:25.500
According to the DoorDash guy,

00:28:25.500 --> 00:28:27.266
this Krispy Kreme
specifically did not have

00:28:27.266 --> 00:28:31.466
the sugar cookie stuff, so
he subbed it with peppermint.

00:28:31.466 --> 00:28:33.133
Now, I looked online.

00:28:33.133 --> 00:28:36.433
I didn't see peppermint in
the holiday-specific section,

00:28:36.433 --> 00:28:37.266
but I didn't see peppermint

00:28:37.266 --> 00:28:39.166
in the non-holiday-specific
section either,

00:28:39.166 --> 00:28:41.033
so I'm going to assume that this is

00:28:41.033 --> 00:28:42.433
in fact holiday-specific.

00:28:42.433 --> 00:28:46.333
So we got a peppermint latte hotty boy.

00:28:47.400 --> 00:28:48.700
Oh, whoa!

00:28:56.000 --> 00:28:58.366
I do not like that, but look in my eyes.

00:28:58.366 --> 00:29:00.966
If you really love peppermint,

00:29:00.966 --> 00:29:02.133
you need to get this drink.

00:29:02.133 --> 00:29:04.033
I'm mainlining peppermint
flavor right now.

00:29:04.033 --> 00:29:05.533
I can't believe that.

00:29:05.533 --> 00:29:07.566
I need to eat a candy
cane to bring me down

00:29:07.566 --> 00:29:10.500
from how much peppermint
is in this. Good Lord.

00:29:10.500 --> 00:29:11.933
How is it iced?

00:29:11.933 --> 00:29:13.033
That can't be right.

00:29:13.033 --> 00:29:16.400
Krispy Kreme just went,
"Forget it, we're targeting

00:29:16.400 --> 00:29:19.166
the most specific audience
with these drinks."

00:29:19.166 --> 00:29:21.600
People where things can't
be pepperminty enough,

00:29:21.600 --> 00:29:22.966
your prayers have been answered.

00:29:22.966 --> 00:29:23.900
You probably have noticed

00:29:23.900 --> 00:29:26.566
Ghirardelli is a very popular
fancy chocolate brand.

00:29:26.566 --> 00:29:29.400
Well, they have their own
Ghirardelli hot chocolate.

00:29:29.400 --> 00:29:31.566
Could be "gear-ardelli." There's
an H. It's "jeer-ardelli."

00:29:34.200 --> 00:29:36.266
Wow, this might be one of the best

00:29:36.266 --> 00:29:37.466
hot chocolates I've ever had.

00:29:37.466 --> 00:29:40.733
It is so smooth. It is
rich but not too rich.

00:29:40.733 --> 00:29:43.166
This is way better than any
other hot chocolate I've had,

00:29:43.166 --> 00:29:45.400
certainly anything you
get at a chain restaurant

00:29:45.400 --> 00:29:46.466
or fast-food restaurant.

00:29:48.433 --> 00:29:53.400
Krispy Kreme, I gotta say,
you get the W this season.

00:29:55.466 --> 00:29:56.500
Beyond the fast-food restaurants,

00:29:56.500 --> 00:29:57.800
we also have a bunch of items

00:29:57.800 --> 00:29:59.100
that you'll find in supermarkets

00:29:59.100 --> 00:30:00.900
in the UK around the holidays.

00:30:00.900 --> 00:30:02.500
The giant Lindor ball is back.

00:30:03.966 --> 00:30:05.600
This thing is great but also is always

00:30:05.600 --> 00:30:06.600
a recipe for disappointment

00:30:06.600 --> 00:30:08.633
because no matter how many times I see it,

00:30:08.633 --> 00:30:09.833
I always think it's going to be

00:30:09.833 --> 00:30:11.966
a giant chocolate ball, and it never is.

00:30:12.966 --> 00:30:14.100
How many Lindor do you think

00:30:14.100 --> 00:30:16.066
you actually get in one of these?

00:30:16.066 --> 00:30:19.666
Ooh, actually that's
reasonably generous. Lindor?

00:30:19.666 --> 00:30:21.300
I like that they've even shaped the ball

00:30:21.300 --> 00:30:23.266
like a little Lindor, with
those little indentations.

00:30:23.266 --> 00:30:26.100
Next up we have a
festive-edition Toblerone.

00:30:26.100 --> 00:30:27.966
This is the orange twist flavor.

00:30:27.966 --> 00:30:29.800
I don't know if these are
as big a thing in the US

00:30:29.800 --> 00:30:30.633
as they are in the UK,

00:30:30.633 --> 00:30:32.533
but people do love them
over here in the UK.

00:30:32.533 --> 00:30:34.866
It's usually something that I
might receive maybe as a gift

00:30:34.866 --> 00:30:36.300
or I will occasionally buy

00:30:36.300 --> 00:30:38.066
in, like, an airport duty-free lounge.

00:30:45.633 --> 00:30:47.233
I'm not a huge orange chocolate guy,

00:30:47.233 --> 00:30:49.133
but, honestly, this is really good.

00:30:49.133 --> 00:30:51.800
Gentle orangey flavor with
the Toblerone texture.

00:30:51.800 --> 00:30:52.766
Thumbs-up from me.

00:30:52.766 --> 00:30:54.400
Cadbury usually comes
up big for the holidays.

00:30:54.400 --> 00:30:56.000
We've got a couple of items here,

00:30:56.000 --> 00:30:58.166
including this lovely chocolate Santa,

00:30:58.166 --> 00:31:00.300
which unfortunately is hollow.

00:31:00.300 --> 00:31:01.466
But you can also buy

00:31:01.466 --> 00:31:03.300
Christmas tree decorations from Cadbury.

00:31:03.300 --> 00:31:06.000
It's a bag full of
little edible ornaments.

00:31:06.000 --> 00:31:07.533
Do not eat the foil or the string,

00:31:07.533 --> 00:31:10.233
but within there, there
is some milk chocolate.

00:31:11.333 --> 00:31:13.400
Oreo also has their own house.

00:31:13.400 --> 00:31:15.400
This is their prebuilt cookie house,

00:31:15.400 --> 00:31:17.600
which is made of their cookies.

00:31:17.600 --> 00:31:19.033
But we're going to start by tasting

00:31:19.033 --> 00:31:22.533
some of their other holiday
stuff, like the snowballs.

00:31:22.533 --> 00:31:27.433
They're a chocolate filled
with an Oreo filling.

00:31:27.433 --> 00:31:30.600
Hold on. These look underfilled.

00:31:33.800 --> 00:31:36.900
Awful. It doesn't taste
anything like Oreos to me.

00:31:36.900 --> 00:31:39.000
Moving on to the actual cookies,

00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:41.666
we have the classic holiday Oreos

00:31:41.666 --> 00:31:43.433
that just have the red filling,

00:31:43.433 --> 00:31:45.966
and then we have hot cocoa Oreos,

00:31:45.966 --> 00:31:47.400
which I've never tried before.

00:31:47.400 --> 00:31:48.766
Oreo is always trying

00:31:48.766 --> 00:31:50.966
the weirdest flavor combinations to me.

00:31:50.966 --> 00:31:54.066
Do you remember that they
did a Swedish Fish Oreo?

00:31:56.366 --> 00:31:58.300
Look at those two layers in there.

00:31:58.300 --> 00:32:00.033
I think that's a fun little touch.

00:32:00.033 --> 00:32:03.233
Like all other Oreos, all
the cream goes to one side.

00:32:05.366 --> 00:32:07.200
It's a better concept to me than it is

00:32:07.200 --> 00:32:10.066
in actual cookie form.

00:32:10.066 --> 00:32:12.966
Now, these I know and I love.

00:32:12.966 --> 00:32:16.466
What the hell? The serving
size for Oreos is two.

00:32:16.466 --> 00:32:18.533
In my brain I'm going to
believe that this was colored

00:32:18.533 --> 00:32:21.233
with beet juice and not red dye 40.

00:32:22.833 --> 00:32:26.700
I scrape all of the creme off, like that,

00:32:26.700 --> 00:32:28.833
and then I eat the two cookies together.

00:32:30.133 --> 00:32:31.266
Katya: Boo!

00:32:31.266 --> 00:32:32.533
[crew laughs]

00:32:32.533 --> 00:32:34.466
They booed Jesus too.

00:32:34.466 --> 00:32:37.366
Moving on, we have the
white-fudge-covered Oreo,

00:32:37.366 --> 00:32:40.366
so it's a regular Oreo
covered in this white fudge.

00:32:40.366 --> 00:32:41.366
I've had these before,

00:32:41.366 --> 00:32:43.433
and they're actually really, really good.

00:32:43.433 --> 00:32:46.533
I think it's time to build
our Oreo cookie house.

00:32:46.533 --> 00:32:50.100
So, it comes with a couple
of packs of plain Oreos

00:32:50.100 --> 00:32:51.666
for you to decorate with.

00:32:51.666 --> 00:32:54.500
So, I think that this
icing is actually flavored

00:32:54.500 --> 00:32:56.633
just like the Oreo filling.

00:32:56.633 --> 00:32:59.800
These little, I think they're gummy stars.

00:32:59.800 --> 00:33:02.300
Look at these little
gingerbread men in there.

00:33:02.300 --> 00:33:04.266
And then we have a couple of tubes

00:33:04.266 --> 00:33:08.400
of red and green icing for
you to decorate with too,

00:33:08.400 --> 00:33:12.433
and then we have the actual cookie house.

00:33:12.433 --> 00:33:15.733
Oh, no! Our roof caved in a bit.

00:33:15.733 --> 00:33:18.333
But it's OK, I think I can
fix it with some icing.

00:33:18.333 --> 00:33:22.100
Oh, no, it turns out
that the icing in these

00:33:22.100 --> 00:33:26.500
cookie-gingerbread-house-making
kits still sucks.

00:33:26.500 --> 00:33:30.400
Skill level one. Really
easy. It's not true.

00:33:30.400 --> 00:33:33.866
The doorknob is ginormous
compared to the door.

00:33:33.866 --> 00:33:37.900
This is the hardest thing
I've ever done in my life.

00:33:37.900 --> 00:33:39.966
They're already all broken.

00:33:40.933 --> 00:33:45.100
Oh, my God, these stars are hard as rocks.

00:33:45.100 --> 00:33:48.166
Stop zooming in on the house.
Stop zooming in on the house.

00:33:48.166 --> 00:33:51.133
And here are all of the exclusive holiday

00:33:51.133 --> 00:33:53.800
Hershey's chocolates that I could find.

00:33:53.800 --> 00:33:57.400
So, first we have these bells
that are peppermint bark.

00:33:57.400 --> 00:33:59.100
It's a white chocolate on top

00:33:59.100 --> 00:34:01.466
and then a milk chocolate on the bottom.

00:34:03.400 --> 00:34:05.333
That is so good.

00:34:06.433 --> 00:34:09.466
Mm! These little sprinkles
that it has all throughout

00:34:09.466 --> 00:34:11.433
adds a really, really nice texture.

00:34:11.433 --> 00:34:14.433
These are the mint truffle Kisses.

00:34:14.433 --> 00:34:17.100
So they have this mint
filling inside of them

00:34:17.100 --> 00:34:19.500
that is green. That we'll skip.

00:34:19.500 --> 00:34:21.400
And these are the candy cane Kisses,

00:34:21.400 --> 00:34:23.266
which are also peppermint flavored,

00:34:23.266 --> 00:34:25.033
and they have those little
sprinkles running throughout,

00:34:25.033 --> 00:34:27.100
so I'm sure they taste
similar to the bells.

00:34:27.100 --> 00:34:30.066
These are the cherry cordial Kisses.

00:34:30.066 --> 00:34:32.966
On the outside it looks like
a regular chocolate Kiss,

00:34:32.966 --> 00:34:35.733
but it's supposed to have
that cherry cordial filling.

00:34:38.166 --> 00:34:41.600
Oh! Bleh! Mediciny.

00:34:41.600 --> 00:34:44.100
So, these are the sugar cookie Kisses.

00:34:49.666 --> 00:34:53.233
That's so good. It tastes like
cake batter, in a good way.

00:34:53.233 --> 00:34:57.133
We have the hot cocoa Kisses,
which are really cute.

00:34:57.133 --> 00:35:00.500
So it's milk chocolate with
marshmallow-flavored creme.

00:35:05.366 --> 00:35:07.666
I know how weird it sounds to say this

00:35:07.666 --> 00:35:09.400
as I'm eating chocolate candy,

00:35:09.400 --> 00:35:11.466
but it's literally just too sweet for me.

00:35:11.466 --> 00:35:13.800
We also have the Hershey's Kisses

00:35:13.800 --> 00:35:15.033
that are cookies and cream,

00:35:15.033 --> 00:35:16.466
which is basically like what their

00:35:16.466 --> 00:35:19.800
cookies and cream bars taste
like, which is amazing.

00:35:19.800 --> 00:35:22.200
Calories per pieces gives you seven.

00:35:22.200 --> 00:35:25.866
You can have seven kisses,
and it's only 150 cals.

00:35:28.900 --> 00:35:31.566
Tastes just like the
Hershey bar. It's amazing.

00:35:31.566 --> 00:35:32.700
So, these are a little different.

00:35:32.700 --> 00:35:34.500
These are Hershey's Hugs,

00:35:34.500 --> 00:35:38.633
and this is a milk chocolate
hugged by white creme.

00:35:38.633 --> 00:35:40.133
I don't know what that means,

00:35:40.133 --> 00:35:41.766
and I also don't really want to taste them

00:35:41.766 --> 00:35:43.133
because they look kind of boring.

00:35:43.133 --> 00:35:44.600
While I was shopping for these,

00:35:44.600 --> 00:35:48.533
I also saw these really,
really cute holiday bars.

00:35:48.533 --> 00:35:51.700
So they basically have
build-a-Santa or build-a-snowman.

00:35:51.700 --> 00:35:52.766
You break the bar apart

00:35:52.766 --> 00:35:54.300
and kind of put all the pieces together

00:35:54.300 --> 00:35:56.066
like a puzzle to make one of these.

00:35:56.066 --> 00:35:57.633
This is so cute and fun.

00:35:57.633 --> 00:36:01.600
Reese's of course have their
own festive shapes, I guess.

00:36:01.600 --> 00:36:02.866
Starting down here, you can get the

00:36:02.866 --> 00:36:05.000
Reese's peanut butter trees.

00:36:05.000 --> 00:36:06.600
Chocolate and peanut butter, obviously.

00:36:06.600 --> 00:36:09.900
You can also get white trees,

00:36:09.900 --> 00:36:11.100
white chocolate and peanut butter.

00:36:11.100 --> 00:36:13.000
This never looks like the shape, right?

00:36:13.900 --> 00:36:15.733
Uh, yeah?

00:36:16.600 --> 00:36:19.900
OK, closer than they
normally are, for sure.

00:36:19.900 --> 00:36:21.933
The Reese's snowman. Get a load of that.

00:36:21.933 --> 00:36:26.100
And the big boy, the chocolate Santa.

00:36:26.100 --> 00:36:29.266
How many servings do you
think is in here? Fifteen.

00:36:29.266 --> 00:36:32.200
Do 14 of my coworkers want
to meet up and share this?

00:36:33.666 --> 00:36:35.000
Oh, man, it's dry inside.

00:36:35.000 --> 00:36:36.066
Didn't you think it'd be creamier?

00:36:37.566 --> 00:36:41.733
No. Reese's has carefully, meticulously

00:36:41.733 --> 00:36:44.833
perfected the
chocolate-and-peanut-butter ratio

00:36:44.833 --> 00:36:46.900
in its peanut butter
cup. It's all off here.

00:36:47.866 --> 00:36:50.700
Also, not available at
the Target by my house,

00:36:50.700 --> 00:36:54.466
you can get Reese's
nutcrackers and Reese's bells.

00:36:54.466 --> 00:36:55.933
Here we have some After Eights.

00:36:55.933 --> 00:36:58.833
Now, I'm not sure if these
are a thing in America or not.

00:36:58.833 --> 00:37:00.900
There was a aggressive marketing campaign

00:37:00.900 --> 00:37:03.400
probably back in the '60s or '70s

00:37:03.400 --> 00:37:06.066
when they really became the thing to give

00:37:06.066 --> 00:37:08.566
to your dinner-party guests
at the end of a meal.

00:37:08.566 --> 00:37:09.433
It's a lot of packaging.

00:37:09.433 --> 00:37:11.200
It feels like you're
playing pass the parcel.

00:37:11.200 --> 00:37:13.600
And the chocolates
themselves are dark chocolate

00:37:13.600 --> 00:37:15.933
with a fondant mint in the middle.

00:37:15.933 --> 00:37:18.766
I mean, these are excellent,
don't get me wrong.

00:37:18.766 --> 00:37:21.633
Polling the crew. Would it be weird to eat

00:37:21.633 --> 00:37:23.766
a whole box of these as, like, an

00:37:23.766 --> 00:37:26.633
evening snack, just to yourself?

00:37:26.633 --> 00:37:28.666
Charlie: Yes. Why is
that ... ? That's not ...

00:37:28.666 --> 00:37:30.900
Thank you. A bunch of
my friends were like,

00:37:30.900 --> 00:37:32.733
"Yeah, I will just buy
a box of After Eights

00:37:32.733 --> 00:37:34.566
and just work through them by myself."

00:37:34.566 --> 00:37:35.666
They do the classic one,

00:37:35.666 --> 00:37:38.666
and you can also get a
selection box as well.

00:37:38.666 --> 00:37:40.400
It's a bit of a one-track selection box.

00:37:40.400 --> 00:37:42.666
It's just various combinations
of mint and chocolate.

00:37:42.666 --> 00:37:44.100
We're sticking on the
theme of mint chocolate

00:37:44.100 --> 00:37:45.900
for a little bit here,
because obviously we have

00:37:45.900 --> 00:37:47.300
the Terry's chocolate orange in the UK.

00:37:47.300 --> 00:37:49.900
We've talked about this in
previous Christmas episodes,

00:37:49.900 --> 00:37:52.700
but they've also released a mint ball.

00:37:52.700 --> 00:37:55.366
You know, I'm something of an elf myself.

00:37:55.366 --> 00:37:56.400
They used to have a slogan which was,

00:37:56.400 --> 00:37:57.733
"Don't tap it, whack it."

00:37:59.500 --> 00:38:00.433
Ta-da.

00:38:02.400 --> 00:38:03.566
Even compared to an After Eight,

00:38:03.566 --> 00:38:05.166
that's quite aggressively minty.

00:38:05.166 --> 00:38:07.333
We talked about Quality Street
in previous episodes before,

00:38:07.333 --> 00:38:09.633
but in the UK, we have selection
boxes around Christmas,

00:38:09.633 --> 00:38:11.366
where you get a box that contains

00:38:11.366 --> 00:38:13.666
a bunch of miniature
individually wrapped chocolates.

00:38:13.666 --> 00:38:16.133
Quality Street is one of the
more popular brands of these.

00:38:16.133 --> 00:38:18.300
This one is inspired by the purple one,

00:38:18.300 --> 00:38:20.466
which is one of the selection-box
chocolates you can get.

00:38:20.466 --> 00:38:21.433
It's a milk chocolate shell

00:38:21.433 --> 00:38:23.500
with some liquid caramel
and a hazelnut in it.

00:38:23.500 --> 00:38:26.166
And then this one is a collisions bar,

00:38:26.166 --> 00:38:27.533
which is where they've taken

00:38:27.533 --> 00:38:29.300
basically the same, the purple one bar,

00:38:29.300 --> 00:38:32.233
but then collided it with the green one

00:38:32.233 --> 00:38:33.933
from the Quality Street box.

00:38:33.933 --> 00:38:35.966
And we have even more
holiday-themed treats.

00:38:35.966 --> 00:38:37.500
These are all from Little Debbie.

00:38:37.500 --> 00:38:41.000
So we have gingerbread men, we
have brownies, we have cakes,

00:38:41.000 --> 00:38:44.500
we have more brownies, and Nutty Buddys.

00:38:44.500 --> 00:38:46.500
So, it's a wafer bar with peanut butter,

00:38:46.500 --> 00:38:47.366
and it looks like it has

00:38:47.366 --> 00:38:50.966
some sort of white coating on the outside.

00:38:53.933 --> 00:38:55.833
It kind of reminds me of a Butterfinger,

00:38:55.833 --> 00:38:58.900
except less good because
Butterfinger has chocolate.

00:38:58.900 --> 00:39:01.300
We also have the Christmas tree cakes.

00:39:01.300 --> 00:39:04.200
These are chocolate. These
are the classic ones.

00:39:04.200 --> 00:39:06.566
I grew up eating these all the time.

00:39:06.566 --> 00:39:08.000
We have a couple of brownies.

00:39:08.000 --> 00:39:09.800
So, this is the Christmas tree brownie,

00:39:09.800 --> 00:39:11.833
and this is the snowflake brownie.

00:39:11.833 --> 00:39:13.266
They're iced brownies,

00:39:13.266 --> 00:39:16.266
which, I feel like
they're not that common.

00:39:16.266 --> 00:39:17.300
And last but not least,

00:39:17.300 --> 00:39:20.300
we have the gingerbread soft cookies.

00:39:20.300 --> 00:39:23.100
These are cute little
frosted gingerbread cookies.

00:39:23.100 --> 00:39:25.300
They're really good, in my opinion.

00:39:25.300 --> 00:39:28.100
I know that gingerbread cookies
can be a little divisive.

00:39:28.100 --> 00:39:30.333
Percy Pig is a bit of an icon in the UK.

00:39:30.333 --> 00:39:33.300
It's a sweet that is
created by Marks &amp; Spencer,

00:39:33.300 --> 00:39:36.133
which is an upmarket
grocery chain in the UK.

00:39:36.133 --> 00:39:38.333
But I think the cult
following of Percy Pig

00:39:38.333 --> 00:39:39.833
kind of extends beyond

00:39:39.833 --> 00:39:42.300
the just regular Marks
&amp; Spencer's clientele.

00:39:42.300 --> 00:39:43.466
It's hard to exactly describe

00:39:43.466 --> 00:39:45.466
the type of sweet that a Percy Pig is.

00:39:45.466 --> 00:39:48.166
I'd say maybe like a gummy candy.

00:39:48.166 --> 00:39:50.566
And they've released a seasonal version,

00:39:50.566 --> 00:39:51.900
which is Merry Percymas,

00:39:51.900 --> 00:39:53.400
which is effectively just a Percy Pig

00:39:53.400 --> 00:39:55.400
but with a Santa hat on.

00:39:55.400 --> 00:39:57.500
But also these are vegan,
which is really impressive

00:39:57.500 --> 00:39:59.400
because usually to get that kind of chew

00:39:59.400 --> 00:40:01.333
you need some kind of animal gelatin.

00:40:01.333 --> 00:40:02.766
I love these things. I
could quite happily sit here

00:40:02.766 --> 00:40:04.533
and eat a whole bag of Percy Pigs.

00:40:04.533 --> 00:40:05.700
Beyond that, we also have

00:40:05.700 --> 00:40:08.033
Marks &amp; Spencer's festive helpers,

00:40:08.033 --> 00:40:09.633
which I think is, like, Percy and friends,

00:40:09.633 --> 00:40:12.666
as well as Colin the
Caterpillar candy canes.

00:40:12.666 --> 00:40:13.900
Colin the Caterpillar has been

00:40:13.900 --> 00:40:17.100
somewhat of a divisive
figure in the UK recently.

00:40:17.100 --> 00:40:18.366
They found Colin's old Tweets.

00:40:18.366 --> 00:40:19.200
[crew laughs]

00:40:19.200 --> 00:40:21.433
We have caterpillar cakes
as quite a common thing,

00:40:21.433 --> 00:40:22.866
like, for kids' birthday parties.

00:40:22.866 --> 00:40:24.633
Marks &amp; Spencer has managed to trademark

00:40:24.633 --> 00:40:26.466
the name Colin the Caterpillar

00:40:26.466 --> 00:40:28.000
and then were kind of
trying to extend that

00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:30.766
to any supermarket that was naming

00:40:30.766 --> 00:40:33.200
a caterpillar cake anything
that began with a C,

00:40:33.200 --> 00:40:34.700
including chains like Aldi,

00:40:34.700 --> 00:40:36.466
who I think had Cuthbert the Caterpillar,

00:40:36.466 --> 00:40:37.933
and they've been involved in a lengthy,

00:40:37.933 --> 00:40:40.033
very public legal battle over it.

00:40:40.033 --> 00:40:42.900
Next up we have Sainsbury's
elf munch mix cereal.

00:40:42.900 --> 00:40:45.700
It's a tasty mix of
strawberry-flavored elf hoops,

00:40:45.700 --> 00:40:48.300
choco pops, mini cornflakes,
and festive stars.

00:40:48.300 --> 00:40:53.233
And you can also get
crackers/chips/crisps-type snacks

00:40:53.233 --> 00:40:55.300
for the holidays. So many to choose from.

00:40:55.300 --> 00:40:58.533
So, here we got the
Goldfish holiday shapes,

00:40:58.533 --> 00:40:59.700
but the cheddar flavor.

00:40:59.700 --> 00:41:01.266
Fantastic. The best flavor.

00:41:01.266 --> 00:41:04.900
You can also get another
"Elf"-themed pack,

00:41:04.900 --> 00:41:08.400
which is the Goldfish "Elf"
maple syrup graham crackers.

00:41:08.400 --> 00:41:11.033
We also have the Ritz fudge-covered

00:41:11.033 --> 00:41:13.533
limited-edition Ritz crackers.

00:41:13.533 --> 00:41:15.166
Cheetos also got in the mix this year

00:41:15.166 --> 00:41:17.100
with their snowflake white cheddar

00:41:17.100 --> 00:41:19.500
and the Cheetos popcorn,
which is two flavors together

00:41:19.500 --> 00:41:20.966
in one thing. Apparently that's holiday.

00:41:20.966 --> 00:41:23.633
Oh, my God, I've been eating
Goldfish crackers nonstop

00:41:23.633 --> 00:41:25.266
for two weeks because I like them

00:41:25.266 --> 00:41:27.600
and my wife thought
she was ordering, like,

00:41:27.600 --> 00:41:29.666
a reasonable amount from Costco,

00:41:29.666 --> 00:41:31.800
and we got the box that
has, like, three bags in it.

00:41:31.800 --> 00:41:33.000
Now, Walkers have released

00:41:33.000 --> 00:41:36.200
three limited-edition festive flavors

00:41:36.200 --> 00:41:37.300
in what I believe to be

00:41:37.300 --> 00:41:40.633
varying degrees of
quality, or maybe sanity.

00:41:40.633 --> 00:41:42.800
We'll start with this one, which
is pigs-in-blankets crisps.

00:41:44.700 --> 00:41:45.933
Literally just smoky bacon.

00:41:45.933 --> 00:41:48.333
Next up, we have a festive turkey flavor.

00:41:52.866 --> 00:41:54.666
I think I'm tasting rosemary.

00:41:54.666 --> 00:41:56.633
I'm getting herbs from this.

00:41:56.633 --> 00:41:58.466
Then I've saved the best for last.

00:41:58.466 --> 00:42:01.166
Here we have
Christmas-pudding-flavored crisps.

00:42:01.166 --> 00:42:02.700
Christmas pudding in the UK,

00:42:02.700 --> 00:42:06.033
for the American viewers,
is usually simmered fruits

00:42:06.033 --> 00:42:08.033
which are then kind of molded together.

00:42:08.033 --> 00:42:09.700
I don't really like
Christmas pudding anyway.

00:42:09.700 --> 00:42:12.633
I just don't want to eat
raisins in crisp form.

00:42:14.233 --> 00:42:16.500
Oh. No.

00:42:16.500 --> 00:42:18.333
All of these are suitable for vegetarians,

00:42:18.333 --> 00:42:20.233
even the pigs-in-blankets and the turkey.

00:42:20.400 --> 00:42:22.300
While we're on the
subject of festive items,

00:42:22.300 --> 00:42:24.566
Greggs also is a place
that pushes the boat out

00:42:24.566 --> 00:42:26.000
around the holidays in the UK.

00:42:26.000 --> 00:42:28.733
For those who don't know, Greggs
is a beloved bakery chain.

00:42:28.733 --> 00:42:30.433
It started in the north of the UK

00:42:30.433 --> 00:42:32.766
but now has kind of made its
way across the whole country.

00:42:32.766 --> 00:42:34.300
It's very affordable,

00:42:34.300 --> 00:42:35.633
things are cooked hot and fresh,

00:42:35.633 --> 00:42:37.066
and it's just very tasty as well.

00:42:37.066 --> 00:42:39.066
They have a pretty decent
range of festive items,

00:42:39.066 --> 00:42:40.666
and we've got pretty
much all of them here.

00:42:40.666 --> 00:42:43.100
We'll start down this way
with the festive bake.

00:42:43.100 --> 00:42:45.333
Bakes might be what
Greggs is best known for.

00:42:45.333 --> 00:42:47.933
In the UK, a bake is puff pastry

00:42:47.933 --> 00:42:50.300
which is then filled with
some kind of filling.

00:42:50.300 --> 00:42:52.300
In this case, it's a festive filling,

00:42:52.300 --> 00:42:54.500
which I think is a combination
of things like turkey,

00:42:54.500 --> 00:42:57.333
gravy, cranberry sauce, and
maybe some stuffing as well.

00:43:00.233 --> 00:43:01.400
Man, I love Greggs.

00:43:01.400 --> 00:43:04.333
Moving on, Greggs has a
Christmas lunch baguette.

00:43:04.333 --> 00:43:06.733
There's cranberry sauce,
some onions in there,

00:43:06.733 --> 00:43:09.266
the turkey, the stuffing, and
in this one we have bacon.

00:43:09.266 --> 00:43:11.133
And then we also have a vegan option

00:43:11.133 --> 00:43:13.400
with some gravy and some cranberry sauce.

00:43:14.600 --> 00:43:16.100
It's OK. It's very dry.

00:43:16.100 --> 00:43:17.366
Being a bakery, Greggs obviously has

00:43:17.366 --> 00:43:18.633
some sweet options as well,

00:43:18.633 --> 00:43:21.300
starting with this one, the festive bun.

00:43:21.300 --> 00:43:22.866
I have some issues with the naming of this

00:43:22.866 --> 00:43:25.700
because this is not a
bun. This is a cupcake.

00:43:27.266 --> 00:43:29.300
It's pretty good. It's
a nice moist cupcake.

00:43:29.300 --> 00:43:30.333
It wouldn't be a Christmas episode

00:43:30.333 --> 00:43:31.766
unless I was mentioning mince pies,

00:43:31.766 --> 00:43:33.300
and Greggs does a mince pie.

00:43:33.300 --> 00:43:34.133
We've had this discussion

00:43:34.133 --> 00:43:36.333
on "Food Wars" Christmas
specials a lot before,

00:43:36.333 --> 00:43:39.233
but a mince pie in the UK
is not made with mincemeat.

00:43:39.233 --> 00:43:41.000
It is confusing. Some
people actually claim

00:43:41.000 --> 00:43:43.500
that the original versions
of this did contain meat,

00:43:43.500 --> 00:43:45.533
so that might be where the name came from,

00:43:45.533 --> 00:43:46.666
but it might just be one of those weird

00:43:46.666 --> 00:43:48.300
British naming conventions.

00:43:48.300 --> 00:43:50.900
Somewhat controversially, I
don't really like mince pies.

00:43:50.900 --> 00:43:52.400
A lot of Brits love them.

00:43:52.400 --> 00:43:55.100
I never really got on with
cooked fruits, to be honest.

00:43:55.100 --> 00:43:57.200
Next up, we have this
Christmas tree biscuit,

00:43:57.200 --> 00:43:59.300
which is very cute. I
think it's gingerbread.

00:44:01.800 --> 00:44:04.400
It is gingerbread. That's pretty festive.

00:44:04.400 --> 00:44:06.633
And then finally we have
a Christmas cake slice.

00:44:06.633 --> 00:44:08.600
This is kind of similar
to a Christmas pudding

00:44:08.600 --> 00:44:10.333
in that it's got lots
of cooked fruit in it,

00:44:10.333 --> 00:44:11.200
but, as the name suggests,

00:44:11.200 --> 00:44:13.466
it's more of a cake rather than a pudding.

00:44:13.466 --> 00:44:14.433
It also typically comes with

00:44:14.433 --> 00:44:16.400
this very thick layer of icing on the top.

00:44:16.400 --> 00:44:17.200
When I was a little kid

00:44:17.200 --> 00:44:18.700
I didn't really eat the cake itself,

00:44:18.700 --> 00:44:20.900
but I would go and peel
bits of icing off the top,

00:44:20.900 --> 00:44:23.200
much to the chagrin of my grandparents.

00:44:23.200 --> 00:44:25.533
This is the Sprite
winter spiced cranberry.

00:44:25.533 --> 00:44:27.533
It's their special holiday flavor,

00:44:27.533 --> 00:44:30.833
which I think is just Sprite
mixed with a cranberry flavor.

00:44:30.833 --> 00:44:32.233
Can I say I don't love Sprite?

00:44:32.233 --> 00:44:33.333
I feel like growing up

00:44:33.333 --> 00:44:35.433
you were a Sprite kid or a Coca-Cola kid.

00:44:36.766 --> 00:44:38.333
It's actually really good!

00:44:39.400 --> 00:44:42.200
It basically just tastes like
a fruitier version of Sprite.

00:44:42.200 --> 00:44:44.066
Literally like a berry Sprite.

00:44:44.933 --> 00:44:46.633
[gasps]

00:44:46.633 --> 00:44:47.933
She's beautiful.

00:44:47.933 --> 00:44:50.266
Happy holidays.

00:44:50.266 --> 00:44:51.720
From myself and the rest 
of the Food Wars team,

00:44:51.720 --> 00:44:54.800
merry Christmas, happy holidays, and we 
will look forward to seeing you next year.

00:44:54.800 --> 00:44:57.800
Please leave us a ‘like’ and a subscription 
as a very special present for me.

